<h2><a id="Presentació" name="Presentació"></a>Presentation <!--and options--></h2>

<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

<p>In case you are required to generate an output PNT file this output PNT file will have an ID_GRAFIC field and another field ID_GR_LIN or ID_GR_POL   which will link to the ID_GRAFIC field of the line or polygon file.</p>
  
<p>On the other hand, if topological structuring is NOT requested, a direct, simple conversion will be applied, so that there will be points   duplicated where there were typical nodes, ring nodes or line nodes, each with the attributes of the line or polygon of which   come on. If you want to eliminate these duplicate points (for example, by the presence of typical nodes, or because the elements   converted were edges of explicit polygons, in which the majority of borders appeared twice) the <a href="vecpnt.htm">VECPNT</a> application can be executed.</p>
   
<p>If you want to join the same file points from different origins you can use the application <a href="mosaic.htm">Mosaic</a>.</p>
  
<p>To convert nodes of NOD files to points you can select all the items from MiraMon and export them to a VEC, which will already be points and,   therefore, this application will not be necessary. If you want to guarantee the topology, convert them to PNT with the application   <a href="vecpnt.htm">VECPNT</a>. If you need to transfer attributes of the nodes to the base of points, make a physical join from   table N.dbf to T.dbf of the resultant layer of points.</p> 

